WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.780
Tie a light string to a heavy one,
both stretched to the same tension.

2
00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:07.360
Flick the end of the light string once.

3
00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:10.180
A single pulse runs along to the knot.

4
00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:13.640
Beyond the knot, things
change: on the heavy string,

5
00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:15.710
waves travel more slowly.

6
00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:19.190
So when the pulse reaches that
boundary, does it carry on,

7
00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.370
bounce back, or both?

8
00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:25.730
In this mission, you'll find out
what a boundary changes about a wave:

9
00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:29.280
its speed, its frequency, its wavelength.

10
00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:33.410
Then you'll follow sound from a loudspeaker
in the air down to the surface of

11
00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:34.670
a swimming pool.

12
00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:39.740
Your mission: predict what happens to a
wave at a boundary between two materials,

13
00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:41.090
and explain why.
